   "C_ab": "C_ab = 2 s(1) - s(2)  (931's pair-complement theorem on stars).",
   "H_Z": "H_Z = h2(p_0) with p_z = <chi_z|chi_z> / sum -- POINTER ONLY.",
   "branch_amplitudes": "psi(t) = sum_z |z> (x) |chi_z(t)>, |chi_z> in Sym^d with Dicke coefficients a^z_m; the SYMMETRIC-TENSOR sequence is x^z_m = a^z_m / sqrt(C(d,m)).",
   "certification_predicate": "d >= 2  AND content gate AND C_ab <= 0.02 (all arms are exchangeable singleton fragments, so R_ind >= 2 is exactly this conjunction).",
   "chi_k": "chi_k = S(sum_z p_z rho_F^z) - sum_z p_z S(rho_F^z)  -- the SAME Hankel blocks as s(k), read through the entropy of their p-weighted SUM instead of the p-weighted sum of their entropies.  This is precisely why 933's overreach audit was right: s(k) is a sum of entropies, chi needs the entropy of a sum, and no function of the former determines the latter.",
